WEBVTT

00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:33.732
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.210
We've got to get out of here.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:01.650
Why?

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.780
Those men are going to blow up this building.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.580
I thought you said you didn't know them.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.090
They work for me.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:07.910
We've got to get out of here.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.470
This ought to bring Evans into this syndicate.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.490
Yeah, he ought to be brought to his senses now.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.720
We're not leaving this place until you tell me what I want to know.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.720
I can't do that.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.340
You've got to.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:16.880
Come on out.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:17.660
Get to the car.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.750
Don't call those men.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.800
Elliot will be killed if we don't get out of here.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:24.500
Are you going to talk?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.220
I don't know who the chief is.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:28.900
Don't lie to me.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:29.980
I'm not your...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.660
You've got to believe me.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.310
I take my orders from a young-looking guy with gray hair,

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.610
scar on his face, calls himself Bordine.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:41.970
Good.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.040
All right.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:44.900
Let's go.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:18.710
Acting upon the confession of Smith, the police raided the offices of the International Builder Syndicate.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:22.140
They found the offices deserted and all books and papers removed.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.180
Watch this.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.970
Smith was captured by Mike Axford, Sentinel reporter, who claims he downed the racketeer.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.580
drug. What do you mean, Clams? Sure, the man fought like a demon. Yeah. Well, Smith told

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.020
me that the Green Hornet knocked him out. You found him and drug him over to the police

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:41.640
station. And would you be taking the word of a dirty crook against that of an upstanding

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:47.890
citizen like myself? Sure, and I would at that. Hello, folks. Hello, Sam. Hiya, folks. What's

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:52.090
the good news? How's the Orwell doing? Fine. Mr. Reed will be glad to see you. Well, I've

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:58.460
got news for all of you. Come on along. Well, you mean you got Ireland, that wildcat well

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.640
of yours? You really struck it, huh?

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.210
Hello, Reed. How are you?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.850
Hello, Fulton. What's all all right about?

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.970
Can't a newspaper publisher have any privacy anymore?

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.610
Looks like we're in the money, boss.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.010
Oh, really?

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.210
Well, anyway, we're drilling into the hard rock,

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.770
and we should have a gusher any day now.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.070
Uh-oh. Wait a minute, Jack.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:12.710
Wait a minute.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.650
Even experts don't predict gushers.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.170
That for your experts.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.820
I'm a wildcatter, and a wildcatter has a sixth sense for a gusher.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:23.320
Those $50 shares you folks chipped in to help me out on

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.880
may be worth 10 or 20 times that amount.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.670
Well, we're all millionaires. I can see that.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.400
What are we going to do with our ill-gotten gains?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.970
Well, I'm going to buy a fur coat.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:38.150
And I'm going to have me a car built that'll catch the green hornet the first time I lay me eyes on it.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.990
Well, how about you, Laurie?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.960
Well, when I put money into an all-well, I just lay down the hatch and forget about it.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:57.390
I just got a report from one of our men at Fulton's Oil Field.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.910
I guess we didn't make any mistake when we loaned him that $20.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.340
five grand to buy up the acres around his test well? Get to the point. The test well's coming in.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:08.610
They struck hard rock yesterday, and everything indicates that they've really got something out

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:29.540
there. Oh. Speaking. Oh, yes, Chief. One moment. Get me John Fulton's note.

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:49.910
That's right, Chief.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:51.960
Due today without grace.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.300
I've asked Fulton to come in.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:55.080
Right.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.390
Ready for trouble when Fulton discovers he's a little mixed in his dates.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:06:59.980
Are you sure that...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.700
the note will bear inspection? Absolutely. I defy anybody to detect the alteration under a glass.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:15.750
Yeah, I've got two men here in case he starts anything. Goodbye. Well, it's been a tough job

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:20.770
to finance, Britt. It wasn't for you and a few more of my friends putting up the money for the

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:25.260
equipment. I'm afraid I couldn't have made it. Fulton, how did you handle the option on the

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:28.760
acreage surrounding the well? By borrowing 25 grand on a short-term note.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.900
I hope there's no slip-up.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.030
Not a chance.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.750
My note still has 30 days to run,

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:36.030
and long before that, I'll be rolling in many.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:37.630
Good luck to you.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:39.210
Thanks, Brent. I hope you'll put it over.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:40.090
I certainly will try.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.020
Send him in.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.500
Come in, Mr. Fulton.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.340
Certainly will.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:56.490
How are you, Fulton?

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.750
Fine. Heard you wanted to see me, Kane.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:07:59.870
What can I do for you?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.120
How's that well coming along?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:01.820
Great.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.700
Be flowing by tomorrow.

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:04.370
Good.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.170
You made me pay pretty stiff interest in that money, Cain,

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:08.890
but I don't begrudge it.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.440
The hundred acres I tied up is going to be worth a million.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.320
That's fine.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.530
Did you bring the check with you?

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:15.190
Check?

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.810
You don't have to worry about the check, Cain.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:21.830
Why, by the time your note is due, I'll be rolling in money.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.090
By the time it's due?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.840
It was due today at noon.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.200
Why, you're crazier than a hoot owl.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.060
That note still has 30 days to run.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:29.980
Somebody's...

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:43.480
crazy, but I don't think it's me. Must be some mistake. The note I signed was due in the 31st,

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:48.480
not the 1st, as this one reads. That's your signature, isn't it? Yes, it is. Then don't

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.790
welch. If you're well failed to come in on time, that's your hard luck. Of course, if you wish to

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:58.440
take the matter into court. I don't have to bring the matter into court. I'm going to tear up that

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.980
note and write you a new one with the right...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.160
Now, hand it over.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.100
Hey, throw this crook out.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.980
The sheriff has attached footings all well, and the cane outfit's taken it.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.070
over. Have you checked on Cain? Yeah, that outfit operates just within the law. Cain claims that

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.550
Fulton assaulted him when he tried to collect his note. He and his men threw Fulton out, and

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:43.320
Fulton, what happened? Give us a story. I'll give you the story. I'll get that Cain if it's the last

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:47.390
thing I ever do, that dirty truck. Wait a minute. Look, on your way, Lowry. This isn't for publication.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:57.510
Boss, I'll go on, go on. Okay. Sit down, Jack. There's your fur coat, Casey. Down the hatch.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:58.570
Trap hanger.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.620
The note I signed was due the 31st.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.380
Now the crooks have altered it to the 1st.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:05.220
Why, the...

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.960
Jack, if it's been altered, we'll show that when we get into court.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.120
I'm not going into court.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.080
The job he did was perfect.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.180
You mean you saw the note?

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:13.980
Yes, I did, and it read the 1st.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.960
Why, he's branded me a crook before you and all my friends.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.840
I'll get him if it's the last thing I do.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:20.840
Oh, wait a minute, Jack.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.390
Oh, let me go.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.550
I'll handle this my own way.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:24.570
Oh, you're not going to.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:25.770
Did you ring, Mr. Reed?

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.620
Uh, yes.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.980
Yes, call the apartment and have...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.520
Have Cato get the limousine down here right away.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:32.200
Yes, sir.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:34.650
And have him come in the alley entrance and keep the shades drawn.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:35.440
Yes, sir.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.840
Sorry, Jack, but get this straight.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.840
Whatever dirty work there is in this deal, we know you're not responsible for.

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.420
And your friends are behind you 100%.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:49.970
Thanks, Brett.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:51.900
I'm sorry I lost my head.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.210
I only want you to know that I have been tricked.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:55.610
I'm sure of it.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.230
There's a warrant out for you,

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.980
and you're going to hide out in my apartment until I can clear this thing up.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.180
up for you. Anything you say, Brett. Cato is on his way. Good. And get a hold of Axford

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:21.960
and tell him that he and I are going to make a little call. Yes, sir. The Sentinel's outside

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:29.240
with another man. The devil is Reed after. Are Bonnie and Sam here? Yeah. All right,

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:29.860
send Reed in.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:31.560
And tell the boys to stand by.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:32.270
Okay.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:35.620
Can you come in, please?

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.730
How do you do, gentlemen?

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:38.530
How do you do, Mr. Cain?

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:38.930
I'm a chair.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:39.550
Thank you.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:40.720
What can I do for you?

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.820
We'd like to know about John Fulton's oil well.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.600
Your man Larry's been here, Mr. Reed.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.690
I told him all there was to tell.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.880
Fulton had a note come due, and...

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.240
We didn't come here for a story, Cain.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:56.000
It just so happens that Axford and I invested a small amount of money in Fulton's well.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.100
Since the company is unincorporated, we want to know where we stand.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:11:59.920
And see him.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.510
Mr. Cain. I've known Johnny Fulton for five years, and an honester lad...

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.800
That's all, Michael. How about those shares, Cain?

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.840
Legally, Mr. Reed, you and the rest of the investors haven't a leg to stand on.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:14.650
However, we will no doubt be able to pay off the small stockholders up to the amount

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:15.250
of their investments.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:16.220
Very generous.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.860
We want to be fair, and no doubt it would be some expense if we were obliged to go to

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:20.120
court.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.800
But, Reed, if the whale turns out to be negotiator...

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.000
It hasn't, Michael. You're lucky to get your money back.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.540
Thanks very much for the information.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:27.600
You're quite welcome today.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:28.520
Good night, sir.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:43.760
Where's Mr. Fulton?

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.280
Sleep now, Mr. Britt.

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:46.150
Sleep, huh?

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:46.790
How is he?

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:47.950
Not very good.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:52.280
Keeps muttering in his sleep about crooks and changing date on note.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.400
Lock his door on the outside.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.390
The Green Hornet's going to have a look at that note.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:28.300
That's safe, Cain.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:36.940
Green Hornet.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.050
Right, Cain.

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:38.950
The Green Hornet.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:39.210
What?

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.610
John Fulton's note for $25,000.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.410
Fulton's note?

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.060
I haven't it.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:46.960
Don't lie to me.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:48.830
I'm not lying.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.450
I gave the note to Galt.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:51.350
Who is Galt?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.720
He's a new owner of the Fulton Oil Properties.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:58.180
I sold out to him and he wanted the note to attach to his bill of sale in case the title

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:58.660
was questioned.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:13:59.980
Then you thought it might be...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.490
question, huh? Where is Galt now? He's out at the well. Get him on the phone. Come on,

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:25.820
come on. I'm going to shoot this well the first thing in the morning. There'll be a truck here

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:29.840
with explosives any time now. Why shoot a well and drill the hard rock?

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.930
It's dangerous, and besides, I'll decide what's dangerous around here.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.310
All you have to do is to obey orders.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:44.950
Hello?

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:45.850
Hello, Gordon.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:46.810
This is Cain.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:51.290
You got that note of John Fulton's with you, or did you record it?

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.780
I got it right here in my pocket.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:54.770
I haven't had time to record it yet.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:56.950
Why?

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:58.900
The boss said it was okay.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:14:59.970
Well, we might want to...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.700
have it around in case this matter goes to court.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.520
Keep it with you. That's all.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.720
Galt says the chief told him that it was okay.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:12.430
So you and Galt are part of the syndicate, huh?

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.090
Now come across fast, Cain.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.570
Who's the chief? I can't tell you that.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:17.620
They'd kill me.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.300
Mr. Fulton's note, Mr. Britt?

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.810
Not yet, but I will before the night's over.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:52.550
Faster.

00:16:11.836 --> 00:16:12.796
and nitro cartridges.

00:16:13.308 --> 00:16:13.948
Where will you have him?

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.000
Right here on the platform.

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:15.800
Okay.

00:16:17.692 --> 00:16:18.872
Don't any of you fellas trip over.

00:16:18.952 --> 00:16:20.092
That'll blow you from here to Mars.

00:16:21.404 --> 00:16:22.464
When do you start to shoot the well?

00:16:22.876 --> 00:16:24.376
Come here, Morton, as soon as the crew get here.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:25.460
Good luck to him.

00:16:26.108 --> 00:16:26.768
Ms. Goodatter.

00:16:37.036 --> 00:16:38.676
I still think you'd better continue drilling.

00:16:39.532 --> 00:16:40.672
You're not supposed to think.

00:16:53.772 --> 00:16:56.592
If you're going to continue to work for me, you'll have to obey orders without question.

00:16:57.548 --> 00:16:58.388
Well, I always thought.

00:16:58.576 --> 00:16:59.616
And mind what you thought.

00:17:00.188 --> 00:17:00.888
You may have flashlights.

00:17:01.404 --> 00:17:02.304
Hey, Mr. Goff.

00:17:03.196 --> 00:17:04.676
Don't move, either of you.

00:17:06.588 --> 00:17:07.268
Green Hornet.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.580
There was something phony about this job.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.280
There is.

00:17:14.172 --> 00:17:14.492
Golf.

00:17:14.844 --> 00:17:16.924
I want John Fulton's note that Ken endorsed over to you.

00:17:17.308 --> 00:17:18.128
How do you know about that?

00:17:18.396 --> 00:17:19.756
Perhaps you told me about it.

00:17:19.932 --> 00:17:20.872
Come on, hand it over, quick.

00:17:21.756 --> 00:17:22.516
And I'll treks golf.

00:17:30.156 --> 00:17:30.556
Give me that.

00:17:35.052 --> 00:17:36.352
You on October 1st, eh?

00:17:36.876 --> 00:17:38.556
That was a clever job of altering the date.

00:17:39.052 --> 00:17:40.472
You're crazy. No one ordered that note.

00:17:40.692 --> 00:17:41.772
Talk fast if you want to live.

00:17:42.132 --> 00:17:43.912
The date was the 31st when Bolton signed the note.

00:17:44.172 --> 00:17:44.932
Don't change the day.

00:17:45.032 --> 00:17:45.192
Quick.

00:17:45.964 --> 00:17:46.444
Don't shoot.

00:17:46.956 --> 00:17:49.096
Can't you disappear in ink when you wrote the three on the date?

00:17:49.452 --> 00:17:51.632
It faded out a few hours later and left only the one.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.580
That note's good in any court in the country.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.100
That's no good to you, Horner.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.100
How about a little slip?

00:17:56.492 --> 00:17:57.592
I don't need a split.

00:17:57.932 --> 00:17:59.912
With what I know, I can force Fulton to pay me $50,000.

00:18:00.028 --> 00:18:00.708
for that note.

00:18:01.628 --> 00:18:02.308
$50,000.

00:18:02.908 --> 00:18:04.088
We'll do better than that, please.

00:18:04.828 --> 00:18:06.128
You're a part of the crime syndicate, eh?

00:18:06.428 --> 00:18:07.368
Who's the boss of the outfit?

00:18:07.996 --> 00:18:08.836
I don't blow in the opposite.

